pack.name=Gliss – Resources
pack.description=Texture and texts for the Gliss block (after Andreas Eschbach).
tile.gliss:gliss_block.name=Gliss Block
gliss.hud=§b◆ GLISS ◆§r  %s m/s   §7no friction · no steering · no braking§r
gliss.hud.stuck=§b◆ GLISS ◆§r  §cStuck!§r   §7Throw something away (Q) – recoil gets you moving§r
gliss.hud.air=§b◆ GLISS ◆§r  %s m/s   §7airborne – momentum is kept§r
gliss.msg.enter=§b[Gliss]§r You are on Gliss – no friction! You can neither steer nor brake. Recoil: throw items away (Q) or shoot. Solid ground or a wall will stop you.
gliss.msg.exit=§b[Gliss]§r Solid ground – you are back in control.
gliss.msg.recoil=§b[Gliss]§r Recoil! Conservation of momentum: you glide the opposite way.
gliss.msg.bounce=§b[Gliss]§r Impact – you bounce off.
gliss.msg.stuck=§b[Gliss]§r You are stuck, just like in the novel: without friction there is nothing to push against. Throw items away (Q), shoot a bow, get pushed – or mine the block under you.
gliss.msg.loaded=§b[Gliss]§r Add-on active. Get the block: creative inventory (search "Gliss") or /give @s gliss:gliss_block 64
gliss.msg.web=§b[Gliss]§r Cobweb – you have grip and control again.
